{
  "summary": "This experiment tested ViT-L as the image encoder in a multiprofile multimodal setup with PCA RNA encoding, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion, achieving higher validation accuracy (0.6287) compared to the ResNet50 baseline (0.6186). The validation F1 (0.5993) is slightly lower than the baseline, suggesting the image encoder choice may influence accuracy but not all metrics. The role of other factors, such as aggregation or fusion, remains uncertain without direct comparison."
}

